{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he shall dip, and sprinkle.</b> For every sprinkling — a dipping." "<b>His finger.</b> It says here 'his finger' and it says below 'his finger': just as the finger said below is the right one, the one of the right hand, so too here, etc." "<b>Seven times.</b> That he counts seven times, not once and seven, in the manner he counts on the Day of Atonements." "<b>Seven times.</b> How many matters of HaShem proceed in sevens: שצ״ם חנכ״ל, seven days, seven heavens, seven earths, seven commandments, the seventh in days, and in months, and in years, and in sabbatical cycles and jubilees, and in worlds, seven lamps, seven altars of Balaam, seven lambs for burnt offering, and many more."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {3 "The acronym שצ״ם חנכ״ל is left unexpanded as its referent is unclear; possibly a mnemonic for sevenfold items in the Tabernacle or Creation narrative."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:55.893738754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}